    <DataNode elementId="AT2G31350-MONOMER" textLabel="Hydroxyacylglutathione hydrolase 2, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G31350-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The protein was recombinantly over-expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;, purified and assayed. The recombinant protein was shown to possess hydroxyacylglutathione hydrolase activity using seven related thioesters of glutathione including |FRAME:S-LACTOYL-GLUTATHIONE| as substrates |CITS:[16227621]|. Although the crystalized protein was shown to form a homodimer, the soluble protein appears to be monomeric |CITS:[16227621]|.</Comment>
